      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "If $h=4,$ then $\\frac{3h}{2}+9=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Replacing $h$ with $4$ in the expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3h}{2}+9 & = \\\\ \\frac{3(4)}{2}+9 & = \\\\ \\frac{12}{2}+9 & = \\\\ 6+9 & = \\\\ 15 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
