      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "If $y=-2,$ then $3-4(3-2y)=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $y$ with $-2$ in the expression and evaluate the parentheses first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-4(3-2y) & = \\\\ 3-4(3-2(-2)) & = \\\\ 3-4(3+4) & = \\\\ 3-4(7) & = \\\\ 3-28 & = \\\\ -25 & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
